WEBVTT

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:10.860
I can tell you,
but can I take your soul?

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.200
Okay, as long as
we can save Takuto!

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.160
Well then...

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.830
Well, I will have you kiss me.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.800
A-A kiss?

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.160
Yes, it's a ceremony for the promise
to entrust your soul.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.700
If you are serious about
entrusting your soul,

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.730
then you should be able to do it.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:13.460
Mikki...

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:30.000
I-If I kiss...

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.160
If I kiss you,
you'll really teach me how to

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.100
prevent Takuto from
becoming a ghost?

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.660
Do you want to go
that far to save Takuto?

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.160
I want to save him!
It's only natural that I do!

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:57.160
Natural? I've never heard of a human
helping a Death Spirit, even in fairytales.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.330
But... But Takuto
is my precious...

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:01.960
Precious what?

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.400
Precious...

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.930
friend.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:12.700
Hmm... A friend. Then I'll ask you,
what is a friend?

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.800
Can you do anything
for a friend?

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.100
I-I don't know very well,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:24.300
but I feel that if there is something
that I can do for my friend,

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.330
I'd do anything I can.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.530
Takuto is a Death Spirit who
came to cut off your life.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.100
Do you understand that?

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.700
I understand that, but...

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.600
But that doesn't matter at all!

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.860
It doesn't matter whether
you're a Death Spirit or not.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.500
A friend is a friend!

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:41.860
<i>Why?</i>

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.900
<i>How can this child work</i>
<i>so hard for somebody else?</i>

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:53.930
<i>I believe that loving someone means</i>
<i>having that kind of tranquil big heart.</i>

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.130
<i>You probably don't</i>
<i>understand, do you?</i>

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.900
<i>That's your misfortune, Izumi.</i>

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.100
<i>My misfortune?</i>

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.100
I-I understand.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:15.160
If you'll teach me how to
save Takuto, then I...

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:21.760
If Takuto is really going to be saved...
I-Izumi, by all means!

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.000
What's so funny?!

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:35.760
I think I'll decline.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.800
Huh? What do you mean?

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:43.430
Actually, I don't know of a way to
stop him from becoming a ghost.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.600
W-What?

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.130
See you later, Mikki.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.230
Please wait!

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.300
I beg of you,
I need to save Takuto!

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.030
So... So...

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.260
Izumi!

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:09.330
If you find out something,
please tell me!

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.460
<i>I haven't disappeared yet.</i>

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.500
Takuto, what's wrong?

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:56.500
Mitsuki.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.000
Were you in pain again?

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:02.500
S-Stupid, that's not
the case at all!

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.860
More importantly, are you making
progress preparing for your concert?

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.860
Y-Yeah, of course.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.900
Good. Jeez, you better not become
careless just because I'm not around.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.300
Got it?

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:15.560
Yes.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.000
<i>Takuto...</i>

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.060
Gosh...

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.130
Why are old books so heavy?!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.200
Hey Takuto.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.330
Huh?

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.230
Are you all right?

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:35.730
What do you mean?

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.000
I mean...

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.300
Takuto, please don't go away.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.430
Please don't.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:52.360
I'm so tired.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.400
I'm home.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.200
So that's it?

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.500
I was wondering what you were going
to say with such a somber face.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:04.560
Stupid, I won't disappear that easily!

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:05.430
But...

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:10.000
My goodness... Don't worry
about unnecessary things.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.930
Just think about
your concert right now.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.300
Takuto...

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:21.400
Don't worry.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.300
I'll be fine.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:39.060
If loving someone was going
to feel like this, I wish I never—

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:39.760
Mitsuki?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.360
I'm practicing for the concert!

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.900
Listen, Takuto.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.260
Okay.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:54.830
My tears won't stop.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:59.430
<i>Both Mitsuki and Takuto</i>
<i>are working so hard.</i>

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:03.300
<i>Each one thinking</i>
<i>about the other...</i>

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.360
Well, then.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:10.030
I'm going to do
some investigation.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:16.530
I might find a hint for preventing
him from becoming a ghost.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.200
All right, what have we here?

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.760
Then, please also give
my regards to Full Moon.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.800
Yes, thank you
for all your work.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.300
Oh? Is that you, Ms. Oshige?

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:30.830
Oh, Mr. Todoroki!

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.460
Good morning.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.400
Huh? Where's Full Moon?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:38.000
Oh, yes. Full Moon is preparing
for her concert right now.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:43.030
Oh yeah, I heard. So Full Moon is in
seclusion doing special lessons?

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.560
She's really putting
her heart into it!

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:50.530
<i>In seclusion? Who said such a thing?</i>
<i>Gosh, this industry...</i>

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:51.860
Mr. Todoroki!

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.460
Yeah, I'll be right over.
Okay then, we'll catch up later.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:56.900
I'll look forward to the concert!

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.700
Thank you very much.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.860
<i>Whatever the rumors may be,</i>

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.360
<i>Mitsuki can't be</i>
<i>forcing herself right now.</i>

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:20.060
<i>If Mitsuki cannot transform to Full Moon</i>
<i>on the day of the concert...</i>

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.600
<i>Don't think about such a thing!</i>

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:27.260
<i>Takuto and Meroko were saying that</i>
<i>they are definitely going to transform her,</i>

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.330
<i>so I have to work to</i>
<i>make this concert a success.</i>

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.800
Ow, ow! So hot!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.060
All right, what does it say here?

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:44.530
Drip one drop of the morning dew
collected from the roses on his eyelids

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.760
and recite a spell.

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:48.500
Okay then!

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:53.260
Mero-Mero!
Morning Dew of Roses!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.930
Well then...

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:09.560
Now, for the spell. S-Susha,
doriapisuku, ekkutirijira, furikapasu!

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:10.260
Hey.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:13.900
What have you started now?

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.030
H-Huh?

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:18.800
What do you mean "Huh?"

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.900
I-I mean... Sorry.

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:25.060
<i>This isn't working at all!</i>

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:26.200
Meroko?

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.460
What are you doing?

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:32.600
Oh, I see.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.700
It's a legend of
the human world after all.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.360
Of course it wouldn't
work on a Death Spirit.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:43.060
I keep on making
a bunch of mistakes.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.360
That's not true.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:51.960
You did it for Takuto's sake.
What you're doing is not wrong at all.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.300
Mitsuki...

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.660
What are you doing?

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.500
I-Izumi!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.230
Izumi, why are you here?

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:21.130
What in the world do you want?

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.030
Huh?

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:28.560
I did little bit of research on how to
stop him from becoming a ghost.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.400
You researched for us?

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:31.300
Yes.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.660
Then Takuto can be saved?

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.060
Possibly...

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:37.860
Wait a minute, is that true Izumi?

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:42.700
It's Mikki and your choice to
believe me or not. Which will it be?

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.760
I beg of you! Please teach us!

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:51.560
This is the Mystic Lily that
blossoms in the Spirit World.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.600
It's also known as
the Flower of Forgetfulness.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.660
When you eat it,
you lose your entire memory.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:59.100
Hence it's name.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.060
This will save Takuto?

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:05.760
Yes. I believe a Death Spirit
who recovers his memory

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:10.030
becomes a ghost because of
the attachment to his life on earth.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.800
That's why, if his memory is erased
with this Flower of Forgetfulness...

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:17.300
Erase his memory?

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:21.000
Does that mean his memories as
a Death Spirit will also be erased?

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.130
Yes, he'll forget everything...
even about you two.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:26.800
Oh no.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:31.030
Takuto is going to
forget about us?

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:34.160
I couldn't find anything else
that would work.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:39.460
I think this is probably the only way
to stop him from becoming a ghost.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.760
Izumi, here, let's eat some
roasted sweets potatoes.

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:48.400
Wait! If I remember correctly,
the Flower of Forgetfulness is...

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:49.500
Yes.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:51.330
The flower only blooms on

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.300
the day of the lunar eclipse
in the Spirit World calendar.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.000
When is that?

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:56.960
It's today!

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.430
What? Then, is there a chance?

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:03.700
This Flower of Forgetfulness
blooms in a cave

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.800
at the Forbidden Forest
in the Spirit World.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.500
Normally, the entrance to this cave
is closed and you can't enter.

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:12.860
But the entrance opens only
during the lunar eclipse

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.000
when the flower blooms.

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.960
The flower possesses
a strong power

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.460
and does not allow
anyone to approach it.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:21.660
It's such a powerful flower

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:25.230
that even Death Spirit power
becomes ineffective near it.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:26.860
Is that so?

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.560
- But for Takuto, I—
- Mero.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.760
You'd be breaking the laws
of the Spirit World.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:36.400
Who knows what kind of punishment
will be handed down.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:38.830
Are you prepared for that?

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.230
Nobody will wake up with this.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:10.900
It's now connected
with the Spirit World.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:15.900
Now Mitsuki, after I enter the cave,
measure the time with this.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:20.100
I'm going to lose my sense
of time inside the cave.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:24.730
You have to get out of the cave
before all of the sand falls, right?

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:27.530
Yeah, if I don't do it in time,

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.600
I won't be able to come out
until the next lunar eclipse.

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:31.330
If that happens...

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.560
Meroko!

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:40.500
Are you really okay? Isn't this
a serious violation of the regulations?

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.700
If it's about violating regulations,
I've already done that many times.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:47.800
Being such good friends
with you is actually a violation.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.100
Meroko...

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:58.200
I also want to help Takuto
as much as you. Now, I'll be off.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.560
Meroko! Be careful!

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.200
It's been so long.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.330
Hey, Meroko?

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:24.960
What are you doing here today?

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:30.300
I bet you made a blunder again and
were called in by the Division Chief.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:31.800
Y-Yeah.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.700
I suppose it's
something like that.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.260
Well, I'm in a hurry so...

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.530
Hey, wait Meroko!

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:44.200
<i>Sorry, I don't have time</i>
<i>to hang out right now!</i>

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:53.360
Oh boy, she really went ahead.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.400
She has some courage.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:05.760
<i>The lunar eclipse</i>
<i>hasn't started yet.</i>

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:07.660
<i>Looks like I'll be on time.</i>

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.030
Huh?

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:11.700
Meroko!

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:14.800
Oh no!

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.560
<i>What a forest...</i>

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:19.760
I found it!

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.300
There it is!

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:23.960
Thank goodness.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:25.530
What?

00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:27.700
The lunar eclipse has started.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.400
Please make it in time.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:40.630
<i>Meroko, are you okay?</i>

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.860
Y-Yeah.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:46.030
<i>Oh right, I can't use my powers</i>
<i>inside the cave.</i>

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:48.430
That's...

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.400
the Flower of Forgetfulness!

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.530
<i>You can do it, Meroko!</i>

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:01.560
<i>A small wound</i>
<i>like this is nothing.</i>

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:08.760
Meroko, run away! Meroko!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:17.600
<i>Meroko, the time...</i>

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.430
There is only about
half remaining.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.200
Just a little longer,
I'll make it on time!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:30.900
Huh?

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:32.600
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:33.930
Oh, nothing.

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:43.600
Meroko!

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:48.630
<i>Meroko...</i>

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:54.000
Meroko! Please return now!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.930
I can't...return.

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:58.360
But if you keep on going—

00:17:58.400 --> 00:17:59.060
<i>Mitsuki!</i>

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:04.500
I finally found something
that I can do for Takuto.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:06.330
Meroko...

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.830
That's why I'm not going to
give up until the end!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.360
<i>What...I can do...</i>

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:22.700
<i>What I can do for</i>
<i>Meroko right now...</i>

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:34.330
<i>Why do I like you so much?</i>

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:40.460
Your voice echoes and
it sounds almost sad.

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:44.930
<i>This is probably</i>
<i>the only thing I can do.</i>

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:49.430
<i>Meroko, don't give up.</i>

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:51.730
Mitsuki...

00:18:57.100 --> 00:19:03.030
<i>- Why do I like you so much?</i>
<i>- Why do I like you so much?</i>

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:06.300
<i>- Your voice echoes and</i>
<i>- Your voice echoes and</i>

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:09.130
<i>- it sounds almost sad.</i>
<i>- it sounds almost sad.</i>

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:15.230
<i>- Up to now who was supporting me?</i>
<i>- Up to now who was supporting me?</i>

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.300
<i>- I realize, now that I'm far away</i>
<i>- I realize, now that I'm far away</i>

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:23.160
<i>- what was supporting me.</i>
<i>- what was supporting me.</i>

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:43.600
<i>Why do I like you?</i>
<i>That's too easy to answer.</i>

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:52.730
Meroko!

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:55.700
Meroko! Meroko!

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:58.260
No way...

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:00.430
Mitsuki.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:02.600
Meroko!

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:06.460
Your feelings reached me.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:10.530
Meroko! Meroko,
get a hold of yourself!

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:12.300
Meroko!

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:13.960
Meroko!

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:19.600
This is the Flower
of Forgetfulness?

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:23.130
Takuto doesn't need to
become a ghost now.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.760
Thank you, Meroko.

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:28.060
No, I'm the one who
should be thanking you.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.960
I was able to get it with
the help of your singing.

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:33.300
Oh, there you two are!

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:35.630
Good morning, Takuto.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.000
Good morning!

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:38.730
Huh? What happened to you?

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:42.960
Oh, this? I had a little fight with
the cat on the second block.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.760
Oh yeah?

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:48.860
More importantly, I was thinking about
the production for the upcoming concert,

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.900
and I was recalling all of
your past performances.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.730
Like, didn't we grow wings
the first time?

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:57.260
And after that, we shined
the pendant at the solo concert.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:02.230
Isn't it going to be your last concert?
Let's make it incredible.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:05.560
So it will become memorable
for everyone who watches it!

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:08.130
What's up?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.330
Oh, Takuto, it's because what you said
was unexpectedly sentimental!

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:13.660
What does that mean?

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:14.930
It's fine, it's fine!

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:15.960
No, it's not!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.360
<i>- After Takuto's memory is erased,</i>
- But still, you're really roughed up!

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:20.400
<i>- we can't hang out like this anymore.</i>
- How rude!

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:21.430
Whose fault
do you think it is

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.100
<i>- Staying a Death Spirit</i>
- that I look like this?!

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.660
<i>- by losing his memories</i>
- You said it was the cat on

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:25.360
the second block, right?

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:26.760
<i>- or becoming a ghost</i>
- Y-Yeah, it's because of the cat.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.300
<i>- by holding on to the memories.</i>
- The cat, the cat, the cat!

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:32.330
<i>- Which one would make Takuto happy?</i>
- Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:11.200
Takuto... If... I'm only saying if,
but if there were a way to

00:23:11.230 --> 00:23:14.330
prevent you from becoming a ghost,
what would you do?

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:17.360
Huh? If there were a way,
I would've already done it.

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:21.600
But you become a ghost because you
regain your memory, right? Then...

00:23:21.660 --> 00:23:23.530
You're saying I should
lose my memory?

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:26.830
No thanks. I wouldn't go
as far as to lose my memory.

00:23:27.330 --> 00:23:28.330
Takuto...

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:32.700
Next time on Full Moon:
"I Can't Confess!"

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:34.260
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
